From: Madhan
Subject: [PATCH] display: support a transient, per-display stylus refresh ceiling

Allow a device input bridge to cap only its built-in display during stylus
proximity and motion, without rewriting user settings. Keep user/app votes
below the hardware constraint and layout/thermal/low-power/UDFPS votes above.

diff --git a/core/java/android/hardware/display/DisplayManagerInternal.java b/core/java/android/hardware/display/DisplayManagerInternal.java
index 8ae295dd7..e690d473e 100644
--- a/core/java/android/hardware/display/DisplayManagerInternal.java
+++ b/core/java/android/hardware/display/DisplayManagerInternal.java
@@ -276,6 +276,15 @@ public abstract class DisplayManagerInternal {
             float requestedMaxRefreshRate, boolean requestedMinimalPostProcessing,
             boolean disableHdrConversion, boolean inTraversal);
 
+    /**
+     * Applies a temporary physical refresh-rate ceiling for stylus input on one display.
+     * Pass zero to remove the ceiling. This does not change the user's display settings.
+     * The caller owns the stylus vote and must remove it when stylus activity ends.
+     *
+     * <p>The default implementation does nothing for implementations without a mode director.
+     */
+    public void setStylusRefreshRateLimit(int displayId, float maxRefreshRate) {}
